---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const toc = [
  { label: "What a skill pack is", href: "#what" },
  { label: "Install from GitHub", href: "#install" },
  { label: "Where files land", href: "#paths" },
  { label: "Uninstall", href: "#uninstall" },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Skills"
  description="Install a conventional SKILL.md pack from GitHub once and materialize it for both Codex and Claude — the same files, pinned to a commit."
  currentPath="/docs/skills"
  eyebrow="Product"
  {toc}
>
  <section id="what">
    <h2>What a skill pack is</h2>
    <p>
      A skill pack is a folder of skills that follow the usual{" "}
      <code>SKILL.md</code> convention (name and description in frontmatter,
      plus supporting files). Modesto does not require a Claude-only plugin
      manifest. One pack can target Codex and Claude together so a handoff
      does not drop the playbook the previous agent was using.
    </p>
    <p>
      Open <strong>Skills &amp; plugins</strong> in the app. The library
      previews skills, target providers, warnings, and the pinned revision
      before anything is written to disk.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="install">
    <h2>Install from GitHub</h2>
    <p>
      Paste a GitHub repository URL, <code>owner/repo</code> shorthand, an
      explicit ref, or a <code>/tree/&lt;ref&gt;/&lt;dir&gt;</code> path.
      Modesto resolves the pack, pins it to an immutable commit SHA, and
      copies a canonical bundle into Modesto’s base directory.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>At most 50 skills, 500 files, and 5 MiB per pack.</li>
      <li>Duplicate skill names get a deterministic suffix.</li>
      <li>
        <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> or <code>GH_TOKEN</code> is used when the
        repo is private, through the same GitHub fetch path the rest of the
        app already uses.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="docs-callout">
      <strong>Reinstall converges on the newly resolved contents.</strong>
      <p>
        Installing again from the same source refreshes the pin. It will not
        overwrite an untracked directory that happened to share the target
        path.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="paths">
    <h2>Where files land</h2>
    <p>
      After the canonical copy is stored, Modesto materializes the same bytes
      into provider skill directories, namespaced by source owner, repo, and
      skill:
    </p>
    <div class="docs-table">
      <div><strong>Codex</strong><span><code>~/.codex/skills</code></span></div>
      <div><strong>Claude</strong><span><code>~/.claude/skills</code></span></div>
    </div>
    <p>
      The mapping is recorded in <code>skill-packs.json</code> (source ref,
      pinned revision, target providers). Claude-only plugins remain
      available beside this installer for packs that are still plugin-shaped.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="uninstall">
    <h2>Uninstall</h2>
    <p>
      Uninstall removes only the directories Modesto tracked, and only under
      approved roots. It does not delete skills you installed by hand.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
